"depassement.f0.q": "What distance should you leave when overtaking a cyclist?",
"depassement.f0.a": "At least 1 metre in built-up areas and 1.5 metres outside them.",
"depassement.f1.q": "Can you overtake over a solid line?",
"depassement.f1.a": "No. Crossing or straddling a solid line to overtake is forbidden.",
"depassement.f2.q": "When should you pull back in after overtaking?",
"depassement.f2.a": "When the overtaken vehicle is visible in your rear-view mirror, after switching on the right indicator.",
"intersections-ronds-points.h1": "Junctions, priority and roundabouts",
"depassement.intro": "Overtaking is one of the most dangerous manoeuvres. The rule is simple: only overtake if you are sure you have the space, the visibility and the time to finish.",
"intersections-ronds-points.c0.h": "1. Who decides: the order of priority",
"intersections-ronds-points.c0.b": "<p>When several rules contradict each other, follow them in this order: <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">1) orders from a traffic officer</span>, <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">2) traffic lights</span>, <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">3) signs</span> and finally <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">4) the priority-to-the-right rule</span>.</p><p>With no sign or light, priority to the right applies: you give way to vehicles coming from the right. A yellow diamond sign means you are on a priority road; an inverted triangle (\"give way\") or a red octagon (\"stop\") means you must let others through.</p>",
"intersections-ronds-points.c1.h": "2. Stop, lights and turning",
"intersections-ronds-points.c1.b": "<p>At a <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">stop</span> sign, stop completely behind the line, even if the road is clear. At a red light, stop before the stop line; at a steady amber light, stop unless you are too close to do so safely. A flashing amber light does not require you to stop: the normal priority rules apply.</p><p>When you turn, give way to pedestrians crossing the street you are entering. To turn left, let oncoming vehicles pass.</p>",
"intersections-ronds-points.c2.h": "3. Roundabouts",
"intersections-ronds-points.c2.b": "<p>At a roundabout marked with a \"give way\" sign at the entrance, <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">vehicles already on the roundabout have priority</span>. Slow down as you approach, look to the left, then enter when the road is clear.</p><ul><li>Use the right indicator just before leaving the roundabout, when you take your exit.</li><li>To take the first exit, stay mostly on the right; to go further round, use the left lane, then move back right after checking your mirror.</li><li>Inside, do not stop and do not make a U-turn.</li></ul>",
