"stationnement.f0.q": "What is the difference between stopping and parking?",
"stationnement.f0.a": "Stopping is short, with the driver staying near the vehicle. Parking is a prolonged immobilisation.",
"stationnement.f1.q": "What does a solid yellow line mean?",
"stationnement.f1.a": "That stopping and parking are forbidden along that line.",
"stationnement.f2.q": "How much is a very obstructive parking fine?",
"stationnement.f2.a": "€135, with the possibility of towing.",
"permis-a-points.h1": "The points licence: how it works, loss and recovery",
"equipements-obligatoires.h1": "Compulsory equipment and the technical inspection",
"ui.16": "Regulations",
"stationnement.intro": "Parking badly can cost a lot and endanger others. In the code, stopping and parking are clearly distinguished.",
"vitesse.c0.h": "1. The speed table",
"vitesse.c0.b": "<table class=\"fiche-table\"><thead><tr><th>Type of road</th><th>Dry</th><th>Rain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Built-up area</td><td>50 km/h</td><td>50 km/h</td></tr><tr><td>Road outside built-up areas</td><td>80 km/h (90 km/h where a sign says so)</td><td>80 km/h</td></tr><tr><td>Dual carriageway road</td><td>110 km/h</td><td>100 km/h</td></tr><tr><td>Motorway</td><td>130 km/h</td><td>110 km/h</td></tr></tbody></table><p>In a <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">30 zone</span> you drive at 30 km/h, in a <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">shared-space zone</span> at 20 km/h, and in a pedestrian area at walking pace. In fog with less than 50 metres of visibility, the limit is 50 km/h everywhere. In the probationary period, limits are lower: 110 km/h on motorways, 100 km/h on dual carriageways and 80 km/h on other roads outside built-up areas.</p>",
"vitesse.c1.h": "2. Local signs take precedence",
"vitesse.c1.b": "<p>A single-figure limit sign (for example \"70\") applies <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">from the sign</span> until another sign changes or ends it. An \"end of limit\" sign takes you back to the usual limit of the road. In built-up areas, the entrance is marked by the town-entry sign and the exit by the same sign crossed out.</p>",
"vitesse.c2.h": "3. Speeding and its consequences",
"vitesse.c2.b": "<table class=\"fiche-table\"><thead><tr><th>Excess over the limit</th><th>Points removed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>5 to 19 km/h</td><td>1 point</td></tr><tr><td>20 to 29 km/h</td><td>2 points</td></tr><tr><td>30 to 39 km/h</td><td>3 points</td></tr><tr><td>40 to 49 km/h</td><td>4 points (suspension possible)</td></tr><tr><td>50 km/h or more</td><td>6 points and possible suspension</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The fixed fine is <strong>€135</strong> (€68 if the limit is above 50 km/h and the excess is under 20 km/h). An excess of <span class=\"fiche-highlight\">50 km/h or more</span> has been a <strong>criminal offence</strong> since 29 December 2025: a fixed penalty of €300 (€250 if paid quickly), up to €3,750 and 3 months in prison in court, with an entry on the criminal record.</p><p class=\"fiche-note\">Speed cameras apply a technical margin: 5 km/h up to 100 km/h, and 5% above. It does not allow you to exceed the limit, it only corrects the inaccuracy of the devices.</p>",
